sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Grieneisen et al. (2007) Nature & Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature reverse-fountain root tip auxin reflux capacitor solved on a cellular PIN-permeability lattice, with a growing dividing cellular lattice and gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 bending (Friml 2002, Band 2012) — MorphoEval overall 91.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py` (overall weighted score 91.5/100, down from 93.2/100 in v2). The v2 field was assembled from hard-coded reference-table amplitudes (circular r = 1.0); Pass 3 solves the Grieneisen cellular PIN-permeability operator as a sparse linear steady state so that all six regimes are emergent (WT 113.6x at z = 52.5 um, decapitation retention 0.925, k_lat = 0 0.18x WT, NPA 1.10x, QC ablation regenerating at 112.5 um), feeds it to the Mähönen PLETHORA finite-volume solver (WT z_MZ = 240 um, z_EZ = 390 um), and closes the v2 remediation item in reduced form with a growing dividing cellular lattice (23 divisions, 26 meristem cells, 82 um/h) and gravistimulated PIN3/PIN7 statocyte asymmetry driving sine-law bending with a Band (2012) tipping-point reset (lateral ratio 1.85, tipping at 5.55 h, pin3 0.52x). Six Lean 4 theorems (3 new) verify the laws; 16 reference-anchored measurements, a 14-check self-test, 10 DOI-verified references and 5 SHA-256-pinned dataset files back the package. Disagreements with literature anchors (tipping point ~2.8x too slow, growth rate ~2x too low, NPA z_MZ saturating instead of collapsing) are disclosed rather than tuned away. Overall 91.5/100 (faithfulness 90.2, reproducibility 94.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 94, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/root_auxin_reflux_fountain_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py at d58a084, image/png, 790294 B, 2535×1950 px, artifact_sha256 74eeebaec44a0a577c78fcc9a3d4600c2a24ee895cb7aee80e52214132761d8a (sha256 74eeebaec44a0a577c78fcc9a3d4600c2a24ee895cb7aee80e52214132761d8a), spec_fingerprint 59e5555082b3fc06ab4cbec1acc2a30766a6392b68c0868814d580bd3ce1a15f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 59e5555082b3fc06ab4cbec1acc2a30766a6392b68c0868814d580bd3ce1a15f; artifact_sha256: 74eeebaec44a0a577c78fcc9a3d4600c2a24ee895cb7aee80e52214132761d8a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/arabidopsis_root_meristem_specimen.jpg=1b962c21e75c8e72..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/paper_citations.bib=02c75a0f0c014f03..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/root_auxin_reflux_fountain_reference.json=1fc68ce109094fc5..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/root_growth_gravitropism_reference.json=7a58cd12797ed0e7..., datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/scout_manifest.json=285fff11a61df708...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-root-auxin-reflux-fountain-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Grieneisen, Xu, Marée, Hogeweg & Scheres (2007) Nature 449:1008-1013 cellular root apex reverse-fountain auxin reflux loop (rootward PIN1 stele permeability v_s, apolar columella PIN3/PIN4/PIN7 redistribution k_col, shootward PIN2 epidermal/LRC permeability v_e, inward lateral reflux k_lat on epidermis/cortex/endodermis) generating a >100-fold Quiescent Center auxin maximum that persists after shoot decapitation and regenerates proximally after QC laser ablation (Xu et al. 2006) | Mähönen et al. (2014) Nature 515:125-129 slow auxin-induced PLETHORA synthesis, cell-to-cell movement, and growth dilution creating an axial PLT dosage gradient whose thresholds Theta_MZ = 0.36 and Theta_EZ = 0.14 position the meristematic, elongation and differentiation zones | Friml et al. (2002) Nature 415:806-809 and Kleine-Vehn et al. (2010) PNAS 107:22344 gravity-induced lateral relocation of PIN3/PIN7 in columella statocytes producing a lower/upper lateral auxin asymmetry; Band et al. (2012) PNAS 109:4668 transient lateral auxin gradient dissipating at a ~40 degree tipping point | Beemster & Baskin (1998) Plant Physiol 116:1515 cell division and elongation kinetics of the Arabidopsis root (cell cycle ~17-18 h, mature cortical cell ~160 um); Dello Ioio et al. (2007) Curr Biol 17:678 meristem cortical cell number ~30; reconstructed_in_script: Solved steady-state cellular PIN-permeability transport operator on a 32-row x 9-file lattice (`build_pin_lattice_operator`, `solve_cellular_auxin_steady_state`) with Law 1 counter-current flux and closed-operator mass conservation verified on the real operator (column-sum error < 1e-12); all six regimes EMERGENT: WT 113.6x shoot concentration at z = 52.5 um, shoot decapitation retaining 92.5 %, pin2 (v_e = 0) 0.46x WT, lateral-PIN ablation k_lat = 0 collapsing to 0.18x WT, NPA 1.10x shoot, QC laser ablation + Xu (2006) respecification regenerating the maximum at 112.5 um (+60 um) | Mähönen (2014) PLETHORA finite-volume solver on variable-length rows with meristem dilution ln2/17 h folded into turnover (`solve_plethora_gradient`, `zone_boundaries`): WT z_MZ = 240 um, z_EZ = 390 um; decap 225, pin2 120, k_lat = 0 45, NPA 480 (saturated, disclosed disagreement), ablation 255 um | Growing 9-file cellular lattice with explicit mitotic division of PLETHORA-high cells at 2 x birth length and auxin-independent elongation of PLETHORA-intermediate cells (`simulate_growing_cellular_lattice`): 23 divisions in 10 h, 26 meristem cells (ref 32 +- 6), 82 um/h growth (ref 180 +- 80, disclosed low), 0.958 cells/h/file (ref 1.5 +- 0.7) | Gravistimulation as a g-biased PIN3/PIN7 statocyte efflux split k_col(1 +- g) on the central columella files with Sachs sine law g = g_max sin(phi), auxin-inhibited epidermal elongation and a curvature integral with Band (2012) tipping-point reset at 40 degrees (`simulate_gravitropic_bending`): lateral auxin ratio 1.85 (ref 2.0 +- 0.7), tipping point reached at 5.55 h (ref 2 +- 1 h, disclosed slow), pin3 bending-rate fraction 0.52 (ref 0.5 +- 0.25) | Empirical CV segmentation of the 3-panel Arabidopsis root meristem confocal micrograph (`arabidopsis_root_meristem_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 1527x513 px): N = 113 DAPI nuclei, spacing 18.34 +- 0.58 px SE, apical/proximal nuclear density ratio 1.118 (unchanged from Pass 2); transfer_boundary: Rectangular cellular compartments with uniform row lengths across the 9 files; growth and bending are reduced kinematic models (no wall mechanics, no vertex/CPM), and the Pass-1 reference-table six-regime values are synthetic calibration targets, not digitised paper data; does_not_claim: Vertex or Cellular Potts wall mechanics, cell-wall viscoplasticity, 3D curvature, quantitative reproduction of digitised Grieneisen (2007) or Mähönen (2014) figure data, or quantitative model-to-micrograph matching beyond order-of-magnitude meristem cell number." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add an auxin-overload / PLT growth-arrest response to the NPA regime so that uniform sigma/mu auxin does not saturate PLETHORA induction (`solve_plethora_gradient`, L334-362; `simulate_2d_root_reflux_lattice` NPA branch, L375-468) and the NPA z_MZ collapses as reported by Blilou et al. (2005) instead of reaching the domain length.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the Pass-1 synthetic six-regime benchmark table in `datasets/root_auxin_reflux_fountain/root_auxin_reflux_fountain_reference.json` with values digitised from Grieneisen et al. (2007) Fig. 2-3 and Mähönen et al. (2014) Fig. 1-2, and re-score `six_regime_relative_qc_amplitude_log_pearson_r` / `six_regime_meristem_boundary_pearson_r` (`run_six_perturbation_regimes`, 2014-grieneisen-root-auxin-reflux-fountain.py L471-537) against those data.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the uniform-row rectangular lattice with per-file cell lengths and a vertex-model wall-mechanics solver so that division and elongation are mechanically coupled across files (`simulate_growing_cellular_lattice`, L542-636), closing the remaining vertex/CPM part of the v2 remediation item.",
            "remediation needed: Speed up the gravitropic kinetics toward the Band (2012) ~2 h tipping point by making the tipping angle emergent from the lateral auxin gradient rather than imposed (`BETA_TIP_DEG`, `simulate_gravitropic_bending`, L641-716) and by calibrating `TAU_GROWTH_RESP_H` and the epidermal elongation response against measured curvature time courses." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.915"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 038 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

